WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.553 --> 00:00:01.680
- [Voiceover] Police say the shots

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:03.175
came from one or more vehicles.

00:00:03.175 --> 00:00:04.866
- [Voiceover] Over 12 hundred shootings

00:00:04.866 --> 00:00:06.964
in the city so far this year.

00:00:06.964 --> 00:00:09.289
- [Voiceover] It's time
for someone to step up

00:00:09.289 --> 00:00:12.622
and stop some of this violence.

00:00:18.477 --> 00:00:20.101
- Englewood is historically one

00:00:20.101 --> 00:00:22.161
of the worst neighborhoods
in the city of Chicago

00:00:22.161 --> 00:00:25.189
and, also, in the entire
United States of America.

00:00:25.189 --> 00:00:27.405
There have been children murdered

00:00:27.405 --> 00:00:28.707
while sleeping in their beds

00:00:28.707 --> 00:00:30.459
because bullets penetrated the walls

00:00:30.459 --> 00:00:32.928
while they were sleeping.

00:00:32.928 --> 00:00:37.138
Englewood is generally a
place where no one feels safe.

00:00:37.138 --> 00:00:39.632
What brought me to the
corner of 75th and Stewart

00:00:39.632 --> 00:00:42.158
was a young lady was murdered.

00:00:42.158 --> 00:00:44.148
Her name was Lucille Barnes.

00:00:44.148 --> 00:00:46.539
She was 34 and she was a mother

00:00:46.539 --> 00:00:48.205
and she was just trying
to break up a fight

00:00:48.205 --> 00:00:50.733
and she was killed in a drive-by.

00:00:50.733 --> 00:00:54.151
I didn't know her, but I was outraged

00:00:54.151 --> 00:00:56.183
and I felt like, at this point,

00:00:56.183 --> 00:01:00.331
if mothers are being murdered,
something has to be done.

00:01:00.331 --> 00:01:03.081
(dramatic music)

00:01:04.699 --> 00:01:05.532
What size are they?

00:01:05.532 --> 00:01:07.524
Some people thought that
it was too dangerous

00:01:07.524 --> 00:01:10.497
to go and sit on a corner
in a place where someone

00:01:10.497 --> 00:01:13.607
had just been murdered three days before.

00:01:13.607 --> 00:01:15.611
We went out, we put on pink t-shirts

00:01:15.611 --> 00:01:17.191
and we went and sat on the corner.

00:01:17.191 --> 00:01:19.831
We got some hot dogs and we fed
people, we talked to people.

00:01:19.831 --> 00:01:23.927
More importantly, we
gave out a lot of hugs.

00:01:23.927 --> 00:01:26.144
So we got together, these
moms who had the time

00:01:26.144 --> 00:01:27.869
and who had the passion for it

00:01:27.869 --> 00:01:30.282
and I felt that, you know, being there

00:01:30.282 --> 00:01:32.311
and being present and
having eyes on the street

00:01:32.311 --> 00:01:33.728
and eyes on the children

00:01:33.728 --> 00:01:36.139
that it would interrupt
and it would prevent

00:01:36.139 --> 00:01:38.723
a lot of stuff that
could potentially happen.

00:01:38.723 --> 00:01:40.836
There you go! Woo!

00:01:40.836 --> 00:01:42.432
While you're doing that,
you're playing a game

00:01:42.432 --> 00:01:46.900
with a kid that you may
never get to play with.

00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:48.247
We want them to grow up together

00:01:48.247 --> 00:01:50.439
so that when they're
older, they're not enemies

00:01:50.439 --> 00:01:52.165
and they're not targets of one another,

00:01:52.165 --> 00:01:54.866
they're not shooting
or killing each other.

00:01:54.866 --> 00:01:58.085
Since we posted up on the
corner of 75th and Stewart,

00:01:58.085 --> 00:02:00.688
there have been no
shootings on that block.

00:02:00.688 --> 00:02:02.225
No shootings, no murders,

00:02:02.225 --> 00:02:05.108
there hasn't even been
as much as a fistfight.

00:02:05.108 --> 00:02:07.921
There's a sense of hope
that they didn't have before

00:02:07.921 --> 00:02:09.995
all because we're mothers

00:02:09.995 --> 00:02:13.162
and you don't want to underestimate
the power of the mother.

00:02:13.162 --> 00:02:15.995
(dramatic music)

